<ServicePage title="Insurance repairs" heading="Insurance repairs"
  description="Storm, water and fire damage repairs in Noosa and the Sunshine Coast: making the home safe, assessing the damage, scoping the work and dealing with your insurer."
  intro="Storm, water and fire damage. We make the home safe, work out what needs fixing and deal with your insurer's assessor on the scope of works."
  cta="Damage to your home? Call us or send the details and we'll arrange a time to look.">
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Making the home safe.</strong> First we deal with anything urgent: temporary repairs to stop water getting in, securing the building and making the area safe.</li>
    <li><strong>Assessment.</strong> We inspect the damage and record it with notes and photos.</li>
    <li><strong>Scope of works.</strong> We write up an itemised scope of the repairs and a quote.</li>
    <li><strong>Working with the insurer.</strong> We send the scope to your insurer or their assessor and answer their questions about it. The insurer decides what the policy covers.</li>
    <li><strong>Repairs.</strong> Once the scope is approved we do the work and keep you and the insurer up to date.</li>
    <li><strong>Handover.</strong> We walk through the finished repairs with you.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Before you call</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Let your insurer know about the damage and get a claim number if you can.</li>
    <li>Take photos of the damage before anything is moved or cleaned up, if it's safe to.</li>
    <li>Ask your insurer whether you can choose your own builder. Policies differ.</li>
  </ul>
</ServicePage>
